# Ownership rules for the Datadog documentation repository.
#
# Ordering is significant: for each file, the LAST matching line wins.
# Lines further down must be more specific than lines above them.
#
# Sections, in order:
#   1. Build, tooling, and templates
#   2. Docs planning groups (content and Markdown shortcodes)
#   3. Product teams that co-own specific pages
#   4. Cdocs (.mdoc.md) files. These repeat the owners from sections 2 and 3
#      and add @DataDog/cdocs-reviewers, so they must stay after them.
#   5. Security boundaries
#
# Shared areas with no single product (for example api/, glossary/,
# getting_started/ landing pages, client_sdks/) stay with @DataDog/documentation.

